---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Meghan Lendhe — Neural Interfaces & Interaction Design" theme="dark">
<!-- Tactile Darkroom Grain Filter & Cartier-Grade Atmospheric Substrate -->
<div class="fixed inset-0 pointer-events-none -z-10 opacity-[0.025] mix-blend-screen bg-[url('data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20viewBox=%220%200%20200%20200%22%20xmlns=%22http://www.w3.org/2000/svg%22%3E%3Cfilter%20id=%22noiseFilter%22%3E%3CfeTurbulence%20type=%22fractalNoise%22%20baseFrequency=%220.8%22%20numOctaves=%223%22%20stitchTiles=%22stitch%22/%3E%3C/filter%3E%3Crect%20width=%22100%25%22%20height=%22100%25%22%20filter=%22url(%23noiseFilter)%22/%3E%3C/svg%3E')]"></div>
<div class="fixed inset-0 pointer-events-none -z-10 bg-[radial-gradient(ellipse_75%_45%_at_50%_-5%,rgba(255,255,255,0.025),rgba(0,0,0,0))]"></div>
<div class="fixed inset-0 pointer-events-none -z-10 bg-[radial-gradient(ellipse_55%_35%_at_85%_70%,rgba(217,155,38,0.012),rgba(0,0,0,0))]"></div>

<main id="main" class="relative max-w-page mx-auto px-6 md:px-20 pb-72 pt-20 md:pt-32 font-sans text-neutral-100 selection:bg-amber-400/20 selection:text-amber-200">

    <!-- HERO SECTION: Haute-Editorial Monograph Opening -->
    <section id="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title" class="relative mb-48 md:mb-60">
      
      <!-- Architectural Monograph Header (Restrained, Sub-Pixel Precision) -->
      <header class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-6 pb-6 mb-16 text-[9px] font-mono tracking-[0.32em] text-neutral-400 uppercase border-b border-white/[0.07]">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
          <span class="text-white font-medium">MEGHAN LENDHE</span>
          <span class="text-neutral-600">/</span>
          <span>NEURAL INTERFACES &amp; BIOSIGNAL COMPUTING</span>
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-6 text-neutral-500">
          <span>RESEARCH ARCHIVE</span>
          <span class="text-neutral-700">/</span>
          <span class="text-neutral-300">NEURIPS 2026 BENCHMARK</span>
        </div>
      </header>

      <!-- Monumental Headline with Extreme Scale Contrast Hierarchy -->
      <div class="max-w-6xl mb-24">
        <h1 id="hero-title" class="font-serif text-5xl sm:text-7xl lg:text-[6.75rem] font-normal leading-[0.92] tracking-[-0.04em] text-white mb-10 text-balance">
          Bridging neural signals with adaptive human interaction.
        </h1>

        <!-- Intermediate Scale Bridge: Eliminates Headline-to-Body Whiplash -->
        <p class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-neutral-200 font-light leading-snug tracking-tight mb-14 max-w-[50ch]">
          Decoupling neural decoding from calibration latency to make brain-computer interfaces continuous, accessible, and calibrate-free.
        </p>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-[1.35fr_0.65fr] gap-12 lg:gap-24 items-start">
          <div>
            <p class="text-xl sm:text-2xl text-neutral-300 font-light leading-[1.75] max-w-[52ch] text-pretty mb-10">
              Product designer and neuroHCI researcher. Currently developing <span class="text-white font-normal underline decoration-neutral-700 underline-offset-8">zero-calibration EEG decoding architectures</span> that classify neural intent across unfamiliar sessions without warmup, and engineering human-centered systems for high-complexity operational workflows.
            </p>
            <div class="font-serif italic text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-neutral-300/90 leading-relaxed max-w-[46ch]">
              "The next paradigm of interaction will not be tapped on glass, but decoded from the quiet microvolt rhythms of human intent."
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Editorial Sidebar Panel with Pure Typographic Directives (Zero Boxes) -->
          <div class="space-y-10 lg:pt-2">
            <div>
              <div class="text-[9px] font-mono uppercase tracking-[0.32em] text-neutral-500 mb-4">ARCHIVE DIRECTIVES</div>
              <nav aria-label="Monograph chapters" class="flex flex-col gap-3.5 font-mono text-xs tracking-wider">
                <a href="#bci-monograph" class="group flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/[0.07] pb-3 text-white transition-luxury hover:text-amber-300 hover:border-amber-400/50">
                  <span>01. ZERO-CALIBRATION BCI DECODING</span>
                  <span class="text-neutral-500 group-hover:text-amber-300 group-hover:translate-x-1.5 transition-luxury">→</span>
                </a>
                <a href="#manifesto" class="group flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/[0.07] pb-3 text-neutral-400 transition-luxury hover:text-white hover:border-white/20">
                  <span>// SIGNAL MANIFESTO</span>
                  <span class="text-neutral-500 group-hover:text-white group-hover:translate-y-0.5 transition-luxury">↓</span>
                </a>
                <a href="#research" class="group flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/[0.07] pb-3 text-neutral-400 transition-luxury hover:text-white hover:border-white/20">
                  <span>02. SPEECH &amp; EMOTION BIOMARKERS</span>
                  <span class="text-neutral-500 group-hover:text-white group-hover:translate-x-1.5 transition-luxury">→</span>
                </a>
                <a href="#systems-ux" class="group flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/[0.07] pb-3 text-neutral-400 transition-luxury hover:text-white hover:border-white/20">
                  <span>03. OPERATIONAL WORKFLOW SYSTEMS</span>
                  <span class="text-neutral-500 group-hover:text-white group-hover:translate-y-0.5 transition-luxury">↓</span>
                </a>
              </nav>
            </div>

            <div class="pt-2 text-xs font-mono text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed space-y-2 border-t border-white/[0.07]">
              <div class="text-[9px] uppercase tracking-[0.32em] text-neutral-500 pt-2">CORE RESEARCH BENCHMARK</div>
              <p class="text-neutral-300 font-sans text-sm font-light leading-relaxed">
                NeurIPS 2026 Brain &amp; Body Workshop Challenge: Classifying 3-task continuous neural intent across unseen subjects with zero pre-session calibration.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- OPEN ARCHITECTURAL TELEMETRY INSTRUMENT: Seamless Ink-on-Substrate (Zero Box) -->
      <div class="relative pt-12 pb-14 border-t border-white/[0.07]">
        
        <!-- Instrument Calibration Bar (Pure Broadsheet Dateline — Zero Pulsing AI Dots) -->
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-4 mb-8 font-mono text-[9px] tracking-[0.36em] text-neutral-400 uppercase">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
            <span class="text-amber-400 font-medium">[ 01 — REAL-TIME SENSORIMOTOR STREAM ]</span>
            <span class="text-neutral-700">/</span>
            <span class="text-neutral-300">10-20 SENSORIMOTOR STRIP</span>
            <span class="text-neutral-700">/</span>
            <span>250 HZ · 10 µV/DIV</span>
            <span class="text-neutral-700">/</span>
            <span>BANDPASS: 0.5–45 HZ</span>
          </div>

          <div class="flex items-center gap-6 text-xs font-mono">
            <span class="text-neutral-300" id="current-task-pill">INTENT: LEFT MOTOR IMAGERY</span>
            <span class="text-neutral-700">/</span>
            <span class="text-amber-400 font-medium tracking-wider tabular-nums" id="confidence-val">CONF: 96.4%</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Seamless Waveform Canvas Floating Directly on Canvas Substrate -->
        <div class="relative h-72 w-full overflow-hidden">
          <canvas id="eeg-canvas" class="w-full h-full block cursor-crosshair"></canvas>
          <div class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-y-0 right-0 w-32 bg-gradient-to-l from-[#0D0E10] to-transparent"></div>
        </div>

        <!-- Pure Typographic State Selectors (No Dots, No Boxed Cards) -->
        <div class="mt-10 pt-6 border-t border-white/[0.05] flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-8 font-mono text-xs">
          
          <button
            type="button"
            data-task-trigger="0"
            class="task-btn text-left transition-luxury group focus-visible:outline-none"
          >
            <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
              <span class="text-[10px] text-amber-400 tracking-[0.32em] uppercase font-mono task-state-num font-medium">STATE 01</span>
              <span class="text-neutral-700">/</span>
              <span class="text-sm font-sans font-medium text-white group-hover:text-amber-200 transition-colors task-state-title">Left Motor Imagery</span>
              <span class="text-[11px] text-neutral-500 font-mono hidden md:inline">(C4 Desynchronization)</span>
            </div>
          </button>

          <button
            type="button"
            data-task-trigger="1"
            class="task-btn text-left transition-luxury group focus-visible:outline-none"
          >
            <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
              <span class="text-[10px] text-neutral-500 tracking-[0.32em] uppercase font-mono task-state-num font-medium">STATE 02</span>
              <span class="text-neutral-700">/</span>
              <span class="text-sm font-sans font-medium text-neutral-400 group-hover:text-white transition-colors task-state-title">Right Motor Imagery</span>
              <span class="text-[11px] text-neutral-500 font-mono hidden md:inline">(C3 Desynchronization)</span>
            </div>
          </button>

          <button
            type="button"
            data-task-trigger="2"
            class="task-btn text-left transition-luxury group focus-visible:outline-none"
          >
            <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
              <span class="text-[10px] text-neutral-500 tracking-[0.32em] uppercase font-mono task-state-num font-medium">STATE 03</span>
              <span class="text-neutral-700">/</span>
              <span class="text-sm font-sans font-medium text-neutral-400 group-hover:text-white transition-colors task-state-title">Baseline Rest</span>
              <span class="text-[11px] text-neutral-500 font-mono hidden md:inline">(10 Hz Alpha Rhythm)</span>
            </div>
          </button>

        </div>

      </div>
    </section>


    <!-- SECTION 01: MONUMENTAL ASYMMETRICAL RESEARCH MONOGRAPH -->
    <section id="bci-monograph" aria-labelledby="monograph-title" class="mb-48 md:mb-56 scroll-mt-32">
      
      <!-- Section Tag -->
      <div class="pb-5 mb-20 border-b border-white/[0.07]">
        <div class="text-[9px] font-mono tracking-[0.36em] text-neutral-400 uppercase">
          01 / RESEARCH MONOGRAPH · NEURIPS 2026 WORKSHOP
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Monumental Asymmetric Broadsheet Layout (65/35 Split with Margin Spec Ledger) -->
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-[1.3fr_0.7fr] gap-16 lg:gap-24 mb-24 items-start">
        <div>
          <h2 id="monograph-title" class="font-serif text-4xl sm:text-6xl lg:text-[4.75rem] text-white leading-[1.02] tracking-tight mb-10 text-balance">
            Zero-Calibration BCI: Classifying Neural Patterns Across Unfamiliar Sessions
          </h2>
          <div class="font-serif italic text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-neutral-300/90 leading-relaxed max-w-[44ch] mb-12">
            “Traditional decoders demand 30 minutes of calibration before decoding a single thought. Our foundation architecture operates with zero.”
          </div>

          <div class="space-y-8 text-neutral-300 font-light text-lg leading-[1.85] max-w-[54ch]">
            <p class="text-white font-normal text-xl leading-relaxed">
              User adoption in non-invasive Brain-Computer Interfaces has long been hindered by the calibration barrier. Standard motor-imagery paradigms force users through 20 to 40 minutes of tedious calibration at the start of every session before any control is granted. Sensor displacement, day-to-day impedance shifts, and non-stationary neural dynamics cause decoders fitted on yesterday’s data to fail on today’s.
            </p>
            <p class="text-neutral-400">
              In the NeurIPS 2026 EEG/EMG Foundation Challenge, our approach trains models to classify raw EEG patterns into one of three tasks <span class="text-white font-normal underline decoration-neutral-600 underline-offset-4">without requiring any calibration at session onset</span>. By projecting differing subject and session topologies into a shared invariance manifold, the decoder isolates continuous motor intent from non-stationary noise distributions from the very first second.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Asymmetric Right Margin Ledger: Clinical Coordinates (Zero Boxes, Pure Typography) -->
        <div class="space-y-10 lg:pt-4 pl-0 lg:pl-10">
          <div class="text-[9px] font-mono uppercase tracking-[0.36em] text-neutral-500">SYSTEM ARCHITECTURE SPECIFICATIONS</div>
          
          <dl class="space-y-7 text-xs font-mono">
            <div>
              <dt class="text-neutral-500 text-[9px] tracking-[0.25em] uppercase mb-1">LATENCY PROFILE</dt>
              <dd class="text-white text-base font-medium tabular-nums">0.0 sec Pre-Session</dd>
              <dd class="text-neutral-500 text-[11px] font-sans mt-0.5">Instantaneous zero-shot inference</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt class="text-neutral-500 text-[9px] tracking-[0.25em] uppercase mb-1">ELECTRODE MONTAGE</dt>
              <dd class="text-white text-base font-medium">10-20 Sensorimotor Strip</dd>
              <dd class="text-neutral-500 text-[11px] font-sans mt-0.5">Motor cortex coordinates: C3, Cz, C4</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt class="text-neutral-500 text-[9px] tracking-[0.25em] uppercase mb-1">INVARIANCE TOPOLOGY</dt>
              <dd class="text-white text-base font-medium">Latent Manifold Alignment</dd>
              <dd class="text-neutral-500 text-[11px] font-sans mt-0.5">Decouples cross-subject neural drift</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt class="text-neutral-500 text-[9px] tracking-[0.25em] uppercase mb-1">DISCRETE TASK ENGINE</dt>
              <dd class="text-white text-base font-medium">3-Class Continuous</dd>
              <dd class="text-neutral-500 text-[11px] font-sans mt-0.5">Left Hand · Right Hand · Baseline Rest</dd>
            </div>
          </dl>

          <div class="pt-6 border-t border-white/[0.07]">
            <a
              href="https://neural-interfaces26.github.io/index.html"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-mono text-neutral-300 hover:text-amber-300 transition-luxury group"
            >
              <span class="tracking-wider">CHALLENGE REPOSITORY SPEC</span>
              <span class="text-amber-400 font-mono transition-luxury group-hover:translate-x-1">→</span>
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Methodological Breakdown: Clean Understated List, Zero Card Boxes -->
      <div class="pt-14 border-t border-white/[0.07] grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-12">
        <div class="space-y-3">
          <span class="text-[9px] font-mono text-neutral-500 uppercase tracking-widest block">METHOD 01 / SIGNAL TOPOLOGY</span>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-white">Uncalibrated 10-20 Montage</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-neutral-400 font-light leading-relaxed">
            Streams continuous multi-channel microvolt fluctuations across motor cortex coordinates (C3, Cz, C4) without baseline sweeping, warmup periods, or manual impedance matching.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-3">
          <span class="text-[9px] font-mono text-neutral-500 uppercase tracking-widest block">METHOD 02 / LATENT ALIGNMENT</span>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-white">Session-Invariant Manifold</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-neutral-400 font-light leading-relaxed">
            Projects non-overlapping recording sessions and cross-subject neural drift into a shared latent geometry, decoupling intrinsic motor intent from electrode non-stationarity.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-3">
          <span class="text-[9px] font-mono text-neutral-500 uppercase tracking-widest block">METHOD 03 / DISCRETE INFERENCE</span>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-white">3-Class Real-Time Prediction</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-neutral-400 font-light leading-relaxed">
            Achieves high-confidence discrimination between left hand, right hand, and baseline cognitive rest immediately upon donning the sensor array.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

    </section>


    <!-- MONUMENTAL EDITORIAL INTERLUDE: Cartier-Grade Silence & Immense Scale Contrast -->
    <section id="manifesto" aria-label="Signal manifesto" class="py-36 md:py-48 my-28 border-y border-white/[0.07] text-center relative overflow-hidden">
      <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 space-y-8">
        <span class="text-[9px] font-mono tracking-[0.35em] text-amber-400 uppercase">PHILOSOPHY // ZERO CALIBRATION</span>
        <blockquote class="font-serif italic text-3xl sm:text-5xl lg:text-6xl text-white font-light leading-[1.12] text-balance">
          “The human scalp radiates microvolt whispers of motor intent. Decoding them without calibration transforms neural computing from a clinic procedure into an instinctive human extension.”
        </blockquote>
        <div class="text-[10px] font-mono tracking-[0.25em] text-neutral-500 uppercase pt-2">
          MEGHAN LENDHE · NEURAL INTERFACES &amp; BIOSIGNAL COMPUTING
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>


    <!-- SECTION 02: PEER-REVIEWED SCIENTIFIC LEDGER (Authentic Broadsheet Archive, Zero Boxes) -->
    <section id="research" aria-labelledby="research-title" class="mb-56 md:mb-72">
      
      <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between pb-5 mb-20 border-b border-white/[0.07]">
        <h2 id="research-title" class="text-[9px] font-mono tracking-[0.36em] text-neutral-400 uppercase">
          02 / PEER-REVIEWED SCHOLARSHIP &amp; BENCHMARKS
        </h2>
        <span class="text-xs font-mono text-neutral-600 hidden sm:inline">ARCHIVE // 2020 — 2026</span>
      </div>

      <div class="divide-y divide-white/[0.07]">
        
        <!-- Entry 01: Springer Nature Paper -->
        <article class="py-14 grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-[180px_1fr_auto] gap-8 items-baseline group">
          <div class="font-mono text-xs text-neutral-500">
            <span class="block text-neutral-200 font-medium">2020</span>
            <span>Springer Nature</span>
            <span class="block text-neutral-600">Chapter 27</span>
          </div>
          <div class="max-w-2xl space-y-3">
            <h3 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-serif text-white group-hover:text-amber-200 transition-colors">
              Detecting Emotion and Depression from Speech Using ML &amp; Deep Learning
            </h3>
            <p class="text-neutral-400 text-base font-light leading-relaxed">
              Co-authored empirical research analyzing acoustic prosodic features, formant frequencies, and mel-frequency spectral coefficients to identify computational biomarkers of affective state.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="pt-2 md:pt-0">
            <a
              href="https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-981-15-8354-4_27"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs font-mono text-neutral-400 hover:text-amber-300 transition-luxury"
            >
              <span>Springer Chapter</span>
              <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
            </a>
          </div>
        </article>

        <!-- Entry 02: NeurIPS Workshop Challenge -->
        <article class="py-14 grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-[180px_1fr_auto] gap-8 items-baseline group">
          <div class="font-mono text-xs text-neutral-500">
            <span class="block text-neutral-200 font-medium">2026</span>
            <span>NeurIPS Workshop</span>
            <span class="block text-neutral-600">Brain &amp; Body</span>
          </div>
          <div class="max-w-2xl space-y-3">
            <h3 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-serif text-white group-hover:text-amber-200 transition-colors">
              EEG/EMG Foundation Challenge: Generalizing Biosignal Decoders
            </h3>
            <p class="text-neutral-400 text-base font-light leading-relaxed">
              Benchmarking foundation decoders to evaluate zero-shot transferability across unfamiliar human subjects, non-overlapping recording days, and arbitrary electrode impedances.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="pt-2 md:pt-0">
            <a
              href="https://neural-interfaces26.github.io/index.html"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs font-mono text-neutral-400 hover:text-amber-300 transition-luxury"
            >
              <span>Benchmark Repository</span>
              <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
            </a>
          </div>
        </article>

      </div>
    </section>


    <!-- SECTION 03: OPERATIONAL SYSTEMS & HUMAN-MACHINE INTERACTION (Architectural Chapters) -->
    <section id="systems-ux" aria-labelledby="systems-title" class="pt-24">
      
      <div class="pb-5 mb-20 border-b border-white/[0.07]">
        <div class="text-[9px] font-mono tracking-[0.36em] text-neutral-400 uppercase">
          03 / OPERATIONAL SYSTEMS &amp; HUMAN CONTROL ARCHITECTURE
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="max-w-4xl mb-24">
        <h2 id="systems-title" class="font-serif text-4xl sm:text-6xl text-white mb-6">
          Designing complex systems into transparent tools.
        </h2>
        <p class="text-xl text-neutral-400 font-light leading-[1.7] max-w-[52ch]">
          The foundational challenge of neural interfaces mirrors complex software workflows: translating high-dimensional operational state spaces into intuitive, trustworthy human control.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- OPEN ART-DIRECTED SPREADS: Luxury Ink-on-Substrate Visuals (No Boxed Mockups) -->
      <div class="space-y-48">
        
        <!-- Feature 01: BulkMagic (Massive 70/30 Asymmetric Spread) -->
        <article class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-[1.35fr_0.65fr] gap-16 items-start group">
          <div class="relative overflow-hidden">
            <a href="/bulkmagic" class="block aspect-[16/10] overflow-hidden">
              <img
                src="/assets/experience/bulkmagic-group-buy.jpg"
                alt="BulkMagic campus group-buying e-commerce product architecture"
                class="w-full h-full object-contain p-4 grayscale contrast-125 opacity-75 group-hover:grayscale-0 group-hover:opacity-100 group-hover:scale-[1.015] transition-luxury duration-700"
              />
            </a>
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between text-[10px] font-mono tracking-widest text-neutral-500 uppercase mt-4 border-t border-white/[0.05] pt-3">
              <span>PLATE 01 · COMMERCE STATE MACHINE</span>
              <span>UHUNGRY PILOT</span>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="space-y-4 lg:pt-2">
            <span class="text-[9px] font-mono text-neutral-500 uppercase tracking-widest block">CAMPUS SUBSCRIPTION PILOT</span>
            <h3 class="text-3xl font-serif text-white group-hover:text-amber-200 transition-colors">
              BulkMagic: Campus Subscription Ecosystem
            </h3>
            <p class="text-base text-neutral-400 font-light leading-[1.7]">
              Pivoted BulkMagic from a generic marketplace into a focused campus subscription pilot with UHungry Cafe at the University of Utah. Architected responsive prototypes, mapped complex group-buy state machines, and validated unit economics.
            </p>
            <div class="pt-3">
              <a href="/bulkmagic" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs font-mono text-neutral-300 hover:text-amber-300 transition-luxury group">
                <span>Explore Case Study</span>
                <span class="group-hover:translate-x-1 transition-luxury">→</span>
              </a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>

        <!-- Feature 02: Omara Technologies (Reversed Asymmetric Spread) -->
        <article class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-[0.65fr_1.35fr] gap-16 items-start group">
          <div class="space-y-4 order-2 lg:order-1 lg:pt-2">
            <span class="text-[9px] font-mono text-neutral-500 uppercase tracking-widest block">GOVERNMENT SERVICES</span>
            <h3 class="text-3xl font-serif text-white group-hover:text-amber-200 transition-colors">
              Omara: Welfare Application Review
            </h3>
            <p class="text-base text-neutral-400 font-light leading-[1.7]">
              Designed an officer-facing operational review platform to audit offline welfare applications. Engineered custom design-system verification skills that compressed high-fidelity Figma prototyping from hours to minutes.
            </p>
            <div class="pt-3">
              <a href="/omara" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs font-mono text-neutral-300 hover:text-amber-300 transition-luxury group">
                <span>Explore Case Study</span>
                <span class="group-hover:translate-x-1 transition-luxury">→</span>
              </a>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="order-1 lg:order-2 relative overflow-hidden">
            <a href="/omara" class="block aspect-[16/10] overflow-hidden">
              <img
